se,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":1204,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1060,"license":{"key":"gpl-2.0","name":"GNU General Public License v2.0","spdx_id":"GPL-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/gpl-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTg="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["closember","code-quality","hacktoberfest","linter","pep8","static-analysis","static-code-analysis"],"visibility":"public","forks":1204,"open_issues":1060,"watchers":5620,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Originally reported by: **Florian Bruhin (BitBucket: [The-Compiler](http://bitbucket.org/The-Compiler), GitHub: @The-Compiler?)**\n\n---\n\nIt seems as soon as I use `load-plugins` with more than one plugin, some messages are not emitted anymore - at least those:\n- `bad-builtin` (I think, not verified)\n- `logging-format-interpolation`\n- `bare-except`\n- `eval-used`\n- `exec-used`\n\nI tried this in the [qutebrowser repository](https://github.com/The-Compiler/qutebrowser) by doing `PYTHONPATH=$PWD/scripts/dev pylint qutebrowser/misc/utilcmds.py -rn` as [utilcmds.py](https://github.com/The-Compiler/qutebrowser/blob/master/qutebrowser/misc/utilcmds.py) should violate at least 4 of those 5 checks.\n\nAs soon as I only load one plugin in my `.pylintrc`, the errors show up as expected.\n\nThe plugin source code is at [scripts/dev/pylint_checkers](https://github.com/The-Compiler/qutebrowser/tree/master/scripts/dev/pylint_checkers) in the repo.\n\n---\n- Bitbucket: https://bitbucket.org/logilab/pylint/issue/713\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/713/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]